The bug: `groups[item[key]] = [item];` overwrites the array for each item, so only the last item with a given key survives. Fix: push to existing group or create new group.

The task: "修复 group.js 的 groupBy，使同一键下的所有对象都被保留，且保持输入顺序。" Fix groupBy so all objects under the same key are kept, and input order preserved.

Fix: 
```js
function groupBy(items, key) {
  const groups = {};
  for (const item of items) {
    (groups[item[key]] ??= []).push(item);
  }
  return groups;
}
```

Input order preserved: within each group, push appends in iteration order, which preserves input order. Across groups, the object key insertion order follows first occurrence in input — but that doesn't matter much. The task says "同一键下的所有对象都被保留，且保持输入顺序" — keep all objects under same key and preserve input order. Push preserves order.

